v 3
d 'DAGY': module to compute with causal DAGs
d
d dagy is a Stata command family for defining and computing with causal
d DAGs: causal vs. backdoor paths, d-separation, minimal sufficient
d back-door and front-door adjustment sets, instrumental-variable
d candidates, testable implications, Markov-equivalence classes
d (CPDAGs), simulating data from the DAG's structural model, and
d translating an identification result into a Stata estimation command.
d Uses its own graph storage (frames + Mata) - no dependency on
d nwcommands or any other external package.
d
d Also install the companion package dagplot (dagy's own interactive
d graph viewer, used by "dagy draw"):
d       net install dagplot, from("https://raw.githubusercontent.com/thomas-u-grund/dagy/main/software/dagplot/")
d
d KW: DAG
d KW: causal inference
d KW: graph
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Author: Thomas Grund
d Support: email thomas.u.grund@gmail.com
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260917
d
